<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka closes weaker against dollar.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka closes weaker against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka closed weaker at 42.8450/8465 to the dollar in interbank trading on Monday against the previous close at 42.8400/8460 amid active purchase by importers, dealers said.</p>
<p>The local unit was quoted at 42.8420/8480 per dollar in early trade but deals were mostly done at around 42.8460 level.</p>
<p>The call money was traded mostly at Sunday's level at 8.0 to 8.5 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
